Execute Phase 04 - API Documentation.

Read and follow:

* /project-plan.md
* /prompt/04-api-documentation.md

Review the existing artifacts before starting:

* docs/01-discovery/API-CONTRACT.md
* docs/01-discovery/AS-IS.md
* docs/01-discovery/ARCHITECTURE.md
* docs/03-integration-tests/TEST-STRATEGY.md
* docs/03-integration-tests/BASELINE-RESULTS.md

Analyze the current implementation and test suite to validate the API contract.

Objectives:

* Generate an OpenAPI specification for the current API.
* Configure Swagger documentation.
* Ensure the documented contract matches the actual implementation.
* Create a maintainable API documentation baseline.

Requirements:

* Use the implementation and integration tests as the source of truth.
* Document every discoverable endpoint.
* Include request schemas.
* Include response schemas.
* Include authentication requirements.
* Include error responses.
* Include examples whenever possible.
* Identify undocumented behaviors.

Generate:

* docs/04-api-documentation/README.md
* docs/04-api-documentation/OPENAPI.yaml
* docs/04-api-documentation/SWAGGER.md
* docs/04-api-documentation/API-DOCUMENTATION-REPORT.md

If Swagger is not yet configured:

* Implement Swagger/OpenAPI support.
* Document how to access the Swagger UI.
* Document configuration decisions.

For each endpoint include:

* Method
* Path
* Summary
* Description
* Parameters
* Request Body
* Responses
* Authentication Requirements
* Error Responses
* Examples

Validate:

* API-CONTRACT.md consistency
* Integration test consistency
* OpenAPI specification consistency

At the end provide:

* API inventory summary
* Swagger configuration summary
* Documentation coverage summary
* Inconsistencies identified
* Recommended next actions

Do not change business behavior during this phase.

The goal is documentation and contract formalization only.
